    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0316" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/389.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Informs him, in reply to his No. 911, that the Government of the United States
                    does not contemplate presenting any claim for the expenses incurred in the
                    maintenance of troops in China during the revolution. Authorizes him to inform
                    his colleagues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
